# shot, then what must be so in it: `x,y=r,g,b` at fractions of the frame (imgprobe), within ten of each channel;
# `x,y!=r,g,b` is that it is NOT that colour there. Every probe is of a flat colour of the interface, and of a
# place -- never of how much of something a machine had done by the shot.
# The material graph open: the Surface end's header, where the graph lays it; the pin of a parameter that is a
# colour, in the colour of three wide; the canvas's own ground; and no refusal, where one will be.
surface-open 0.6878125,0.4538889=0,120,212 0.5484375,0.3894444=232,190,92 0.3128125,0.7783333=31,31,31 0.4815625,0.4538889!=241,76,76
# A colour drawn out to the surface's alpha, which is a number: refused, and said -- the bar at the left of the
# words, in the colour of what is wrong -- and nothing under the expression yet. **The words are centred on the
# link, so the bar is where their width puts it**: a change to that sentence in English moves this probe, and
# the two that say the refusal is NOT there with it.
surface-refused 0.4815625,0.4538889=241,76,76 0.4784375,0.6538889!=241,76,76
# The list a node is added from, with two letters typed: the field they are in, and the row the keys are on.
surface-list 0.3753125,0.6861111=48,48,48 0.3753125,0.7338889=14,62,99
# A line typed wrong, saved and compiled: the compiler's words under the node whose line it is, by their bar;
# the refusal gone at the press that came after it; and the graph still the graph.
surface-error 0.4784375,0.6538889=241,76,76 0.4815625,0.4538889!=241,76,76 0.6878125,0.4538889=0,120,212
